// Title: Potential Registry Persistence Attempt Via Windows Telemetry
// Sigma ID: 73a883d0-0348-4be4-a8d8-51031c2564f8
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Lednyov Alexey, oscd.community, Sreeman
// Date: 2020-10-16 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, T1053.005
// Description: Detects potential persistence behavior using the windows telemetry registry key. Windows
//   telemetry makes use of the binary CompatTelRunner.exe to run a variety of commands and perform
//   the actual telemetry collections. This binary was created to be easily extensible, and to that
//   end, it relies on the registry to instruct on which commands to run. The problem is, it will run
//   any arbitrary command without restriction of location or type.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.trustedsec.com/blog/abusing-windows-telemetry-for-persistence/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_telemetry_persistence.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\AppCompatFlags\\TelemetryController.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "\\Command" and (RegistryValueData contains ".bat" or RegistryValueData contains ".bin" or RegistryValueData contains ".cmd" or RegistryValueData contains ".dat" or RegistryValueData contains ".dll" or RegistryValueData contains ".exe" or RegistryValueData contains ".hta" or RegistryValueData contains ".jar" or RegistryValueData contains ".js" or RegistryValueData contains ".msi" or RegistryValueData contains ".ps" or RegistryValueData contains ".sh" or RegistryValueData contains ".vb")) and (not((RegistryValueData contains "\\system32\\CompatTelRunner.exe" or RegistryValueData contains "\\system32\\DeviceCensus.exe")))
